WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.550 align:start position:0%
 
good afternoon everyone  i'm happy to be here  at the headquarters of nato for the  first time  as canada's minister of national defense  i've just met with  the secretary general  we discussed the situation in ukraine  we also discussed canada's contribution  to nato  finally we discussed arctic sovereignty  and the importance of arctic sovereignty  for the security  of canada north america  and the broader  worldwide security situation  i'm happy to answer your questions good  afternoon my name is mark from  associated press last i heard canada had  about 200 troops in ukraine  how are you feeling right now is that  enough troops for what your mission is  uh do you feel like maybe more  troops are in the future  well thank you for the question  last wednesday we committed to expanding  and extending our current operation in  ukraine which consists of 200 troops or  so on the ground we committed to  increasing our capacity to 400 troops  with 60 troops leaving in the coming  days  from canada  we also  committed 340 million dollars to  expanding that mission  as well as additional forms of aid and  support  for cyber security and cyber  surveillance  so our approach to ukraine is strong  stable and methodical we have been on  the ground there since 2015 and we will  continue to support the international  rules-based order in a strong secure and  sovereign ukraine  we are continually examining our  contribution not only in ukraine but  also under operation reassurance which  has  approximately 900 canadian armed forces  able to be deployed to central and  eastern europe we currently are  also  making sure that from a global strategic  standpoint we are able to be supporting  our  obligations to nato the international  rules based order as well as the  territorial integrity of ukraine this is  an ongoing situation this did not start  in november 2021  since the russian invasion of crimea in  2014 canada has been committed we  started with operation unifier we also  in addition to those military issues and  approaches that i just outlined  committed 120 million dollars of a loan  as well as 50 million dollars in  economic and humanitarian aid last week  so in other words our support for  ukraine is ongoing it's comprehensive  but we will continue to examine the  situation as it evolves  nato is  reinforcing its eastern border what's  the purpose of that right now  well the most important  piece of information that we should  all recognize is that there has been  an increasing presence of russian troops  along that eastern border  and as well as the border with belarus  and the importance of a strong  nato  commitment at the current time  is undeniable why because  at the current time  nato is being tested  and it is incumbent upon all of us as  nato members  to  ensure that we are doing our part  for the protection of a strong secure  and stable  ukraine is an answer from the from  russia on the answer from nato and uh on  the contract of nato and the u.s  um what's your first impression of the  reaction of the russian zone  impression is that at the current time  russia has an important  choice to make  it can choose to negotiate with a view  to de-escalation  or it can face  harsh economic sanctions  that is the choice on the table  that is what needs to be addressed at  the current time we are all very much  hoping for a diplomatic solution and  that is  something that is now in russia's court  to decide  what's your assessment of the  chances of the russian invasion of  ukraine  at the current time as i mentioned  we are hoping for a diplomatic solution  but at the same time we do need to  prepare for all eventualities  and what that has meant from a canadian  perspective  is that we have moved the canadian armed  forces  to  the west of the dinipro river  and we have undertaken some evacuation  of non-essential staff and families from  our embassy  at the same time  we are committing  to support ukraine  with additional trainers on the ground  with non-lethal equipment  with financial aid  and so you can see that the security of  ukraine and the stability of ukraine in  this very concerning and very fluid  moment is top of mind for me as minister  of national defense  as well as for our country  it has begun to arrive already  and in terms of what difference it will  make let me lay out for you what some of  this aid consists of and then you'll be  able to see for yourself  how important it would be surveillance  equipment night vision equipment goggles  mobile hospitals  equipment that would be used in the case  of detonation of explosives  these are all very important aspects of  ensuring  preparedness and canada stands ready to  support with this non-lethal aid  and as i said it has begun to arrive  already in  the black sea ukraine  canada will do its part as a member of  nato as well as on a bilateral basis to  support the international rules-based  order which has been in place since the  end of the second world war we make no  mistake that at the current time there  is a very threatening situation at the  border at the same time we need to  ensure that  we recognize that operation unifier is a  training mission  we are  and have been training russian uh  ukrainian soldiers for the past seven  years how many  over 30 000 ukrainian soldiers have been  trained by the canadian armed forces  including 2 000  members of the ukrainian national guard  if you think about that type of  contribution  and the longevity of it in terms of  ukraine's preparedness  i think that you will  hopefully come to the realization that  it is significant  [Music]  [Music]  concerning liquid by natural gas  does canada have more to offer europe  because europe is looking also for  energy security  as minister of national defense my role  has primarily been in the support that  the canadian armed forces can offer  ukraine at this time i know that my  colleague minister jolie and  minister freeland are both working on a  number of additional options together  with our government  including the various ones that you  mentioned last question  have you been in contact with russia  since lincoln sent the answers of the  united states on the questionnaire of  russia  actually my focus has been on ensuring a  strong and  stable alliance in response to the very  concerning situation in ukraine i have  spoken with a number of my nato  colleagues  including the united states the united  kingdom  spain  portugal denmark  and canada's role  is to be  a bridge builder from a transatlantic  perspective  in terms of solidifying  the  very important  support  for ukraine in this particular moment in  time it is a role that we have  historically played and it is a role  that we will continue to play and i look  forward to coming back to brussels in  two weeks for a meeting of defense  ministers where we will continue this  very important conversation but make no  mistake canada stands ready to continue  to support and uphold the international  rules-based order and the territorial  integrity of ukraine  thank you

